s at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"yenc-binhex\", \"concept\": \"yEnc and BinHex 4.0 binary-to-text encodings\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Retro wrappers. yEnc: '=ybegin ... name=' header, bytes = (c - 42) % 256, '=' escapes subtract 64 more, '=yend size= crc32='. BinHex 4.0: '(This file must be converted with BinHex 4.0)' then ':...:' 6-bit alphabet '!\\\"#$%&'()*+,-012345689@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNPQRSTUVXYZ[`abcdefhijklmpqr', RLE90 (0x90 marker), header + data fork + CRCs; binascii.a2b_hqx is gone in 3.11+, so ship a small decoder.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zalgo-combining-strip\", \"concept\": \"zalgo / combining-mark noise and NFD-decomposed text\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Strip unicodedata.combining() > 0 after NFD; then the normal pipeline. Cue: base letters buried under stacked U+0300-036F marks. Tiny decoder + fixture; register in CANDIDATES.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"middle-endian-pdp\", \"concept\": \"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words: UTF-32 or u32 char codes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Given up after 2 prebuild attempts (attempt 1 failed the lib lint: '__import__() not allowed'). Byte-order family closed at D20; if a PDP/middle-endian day ever comes: try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM (00 00 fe ff -> fe ff 00 00 ...) is the cue.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base92 / CyberChef From Base92 decode it; cue = printable minus double-quote and backtick.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base2048 / base32768\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base65536; others need pip (base2048) - install only if seen.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / AD