 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads / #RRGGBB / 4e69:6365 . IPv4 / colour / IPv6 bytes;  base64-ish that won't decode -> undo rev/rot13/atbash 1st (U4fV = rot13 H4sI)\n only A D F G X (V) -> ADFGX/ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  only A C G T -> DNA 2-bit / codon\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX -> chr(int(h,16));  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11);  [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad -> base62 (x1.34) / base36 one case (x1.55)\n no 0 O I l + / = ................. base58 (x1.37)\n 0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: ....... base45 (x1.5)\n ! .. u (+z), maybe <~ ~> ......... ascii85;  RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> base85; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA\nNON-ASCII:\n U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ .. NFKC normalize\n ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ ...... upside-down (chepy from_upside_down, then maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx, spaces kept -> ROT8000;  dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048;  emoji 1/byte -> base100;  CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> zero-width stego;  ASCII-looking with odd bytes -> homoglyphs (Cyrillic)\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English ............... Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also shifted by 5 -> ROT18/ROT5\n mirror a<->z ..................... Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic ................ Beaufort; no period but primer then plaintext -> autokey\n crib map consistent, not affine .. keyword substitution (21 letters from crib)\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3):\n rail fence (D18: number in prompt = rails; w.rail_solve) | redefence | scytale/columnar (w.col_solve) | route/Caesar box\n | skip k | riffle | word order. Strip only \\r\\n (spaces are ciphertext); accept only text STARTING `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\nTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \"Three rails\"); verify on the crib.\n\"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\"/\"This time ...\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned (order, alphabet, compressor).\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18 line 18 = 6-8 char rail-3 slug\n tail); D19/D20 lines 19/20 each have their OWN BOM (LE and BE in one blob); D21/D22 lines 21/22 = own gzip / zlib streams. STACKS (D16-17, D19-21): output hex/digits/b32/a-p/NUL-rhythm/compressed-magic bytes -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"zlib-header-sweep\", \"concept\": \"zlib header knobs under a text wrapper: smaller-window CMF (08..68), any level byte, FDICT preset dictionary, raw deflate\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Knob on D22 (zlib 78da in base64). The carried D21/D22 solver `_b64z` sniffs zlib by `startswith(b'\\\\x78')` only, so CMF 0x48/0x58/0x68 (b64 'SI'/'WI'/'aI'), FDICT streams and headerless deflate fall through to rot-N garbage. Build warmups_codecs.zlib_any(b): RFC 1950 check (b[0]&15==8, b[0]>>4<=7, (b[0]<<8|b[1])%31==0) -> zlib.decompress; FDICT (b[1]&0x20) -> decompressobj(zdict=...) trying the known crib sentence and the title words; else zlib.decompress(b,-15); else decompressobj(47). Wire it into decode_chunk's base64/hex/b32 branches and as a free codec for 12-24 char Mastery fragments. Fixtures: wbits 9..15 x levels 1/6/9, FDICT with crib dict, raw, each under std/url b64\n  {\"id\": \"flask-itsdangerous-cookie\", \"concept\": \"Flask/itsdangerous signed session cookie (.eJ... = zlib payload) and Django signing tokens\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Familiar wrapper' + deflate in the most common web form: '.eJ<b64url zlib>.<ts>.<sig>' (leading dot = compressed), uncompressed 'eyJ...' variant, Django 'eJ...:ts:sig'. Build warmups_codecs.signed_cookie_dec(t): split on '.'/':', urlsafe-b64 re-pad part 0, zlib if dotted, JSON-decode, return the first string value that holds the slug (or the whole JSON text for the slug gate). Fixtures: compressed/uncompressed, with/without timestamp, Mastery fragments (a fragment may be only the '.eJ..' part).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"saml-redirect-deflate\", \"concept\": \"URL-encoded base64 of RAW deflate (SAML HTTP-Redirect), optionally inside a query string\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Stacks three seen layers (D7 %XX, D1 base64, D22 deflate) with the zlib header removed. Cues: %2B/%2F/%3D inside b64-ish text, 'SAMLRequest=' / 'data=' keys, b64 that decodes to no magic. Pipeline: parse_qs if '=' and '&' -> unquote (also unquote_plus) -> b64 (std/url, re-pad) -> zlib.decompress(b,-15) / 15 / 31 -> UTF-8 (or XML: take text/attributes holding the slug). Fixtures: raw/zlib/gzip x quoted/unquoted x query/bare.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-jose-segments\", \"concept\": \"JWT/JWS/JWE compact tokens (eyJ...), JWE zip=DEF raw-deflated payload\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Familiar wrapper' and a D11 base64url callback. Split on '.', urlsafe-b64 each part (re-pad), JSON-load header/payload; if header has zip:'DEF' inflate the payload with wbits -15; search every claim string for the slug. Signature is ignored (never needed). Fixtures: alg none/HS256, nested JSON claim, zip:DEF, Mastery fragment = one segment.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"byte-family-mastery-cost\", \"concept\": \"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch did 0.34 s. D22 Mastery (108 x 22) passed first try with the D21 solver unchanged (plus the solverrt partial-emit wrapper) but solve took 15.9 s and submit 11.8 s -- profile per set if D23 grows it further. Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pdf-filter-chain\", \"concept\": \"PDF stream filter chains: ASCII85Decode / ASCIIHexDecode / FlateDecode / LZWDecode / RunLengthDecode\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Document-flavoured 'inflate'. Parse '/Filter [...]' (or single name) and apply in order to the bytes between 'stream\\\\r?\\\\n' and 'endstream': base64.a85decode(adobe=True) for '<~..~>', hex until '>', zlib.decompress (+ wbits fallbacks), PDF LZW with early change, RLE (len byte <128 copy, >128 repeat, 128 EOD). Also accept a bare '<~...~>' a85 of zlib. Fixtures: each filter and 2-3 filter chains, with and without the PDF skeleton.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xor-over-compressed-magic\", \"concept\": \"XOR (single/multi-byte) over a compressed/wrapped stream, key recovered from known magic bytes\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Joins the new compression family with a keyed step: after the wrapper decode the bytes show no magic; XOR the first bytes with candidate headers (gzip 1f8b0800000000000203 = 10 known bytes, zlib 78da/789c/7801, zip 504b0304, bz2 425a6839) to get a key, find its period (1..10), decrypt, decompress, slug-gate. Also the reverse order (XOR of the plaintext, then compressed) is already xorkey_solve's job -- route the inflated text into it. Fixtures: key len 1/2/4/8 x gzip/zlib x b64/hex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"openssl-salted-envelope\", \"concept\": \"OpenSSL enc 'Salted__' envelope (U2FsdGVkX1...) with a passphrase from the title/prompt\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The most 'familiar' encrypted wrapper. Detect b64 'U2FsdGVkX1' / bytes 'Salted__'. Derive key/iv with EVP_BytesToKey (MD5 and SHA-256) and PBKDF2-SHA256 (10000 iters, -pbkdf2 default), ciphers aes-128/192/256-cbc, aes-256-ctr, des-ede3-cbc, rc4; passphrases = every title/prompt word in several cases + 'password'/'infected'/'huntress'. pycryptodome (Crypto) is in .venv -- guard the import. Crib-gated; output may be compressed (run decompress_sweep).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"serialization-wrappers\", \"concept\": \"serialization formats as the wrapper: pickle, marshal, msgpack, BSON, CBOR, protobuf wire, Java serialization, PHP serialize, .NET BinaryFormatter\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Wrapper'/'package' puns. NEVER unpickle/deserialize untrusted bytes: use pickletools.genops / a tiny msgpack-CBOR-BSON-protobuf wire walker / regex for PHP 's:N:\\\"...\\\"' and Java TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) to pull out strings, then slug-gate (and run decode_chunk on each string). Cues: b64 'gASV'/'gAN' (pickle), 'rO0AB' (Java), 'AAEAAAD/////' (.NET), 0x82-0x8f/0xa0-0xbf leading bytes (msgpack map/str), BSON int32 length + 0x02 type.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"inflate-container-headers\", \"concept\": \"inflate-then-header containers: git loose objects (blob N\\\\0), PNG zTXt/iTXt chunks, HTTP chunked + Content-Encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Same zlib as D22 but the inflated bytes carry a container header the slug gate may still find (but a strict 'starts with Nice work' gate would reject). After every decompress strip 'blob|tree|commit <len>\\\\0'; parse PNG chunks and inflate zTXt / compressed iTXt; de-chunk 'Transfer-Encoding: chunked' bodies (hex size lines) then apply Content-Encoding gzip/deflate/br. Fixtures for each.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rle-lzw-text-compression\", \"concept\": \"text-level compression: run-length encoding, LZ77 tuples, LZW code lists, Huffman with an included code table\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Keyless 'pressure'/'squeeze' puns without binary bytes. RLE both orders ('3a2b' / 'a3b2', count>=1, digits escaped?); LZ77 '(o,l,c)' tuples; LZW = integer list whose first values are ASCII codes and later ones >= 256 (initial dict 256, also 8-bit+clear-code variants); Huffman: a '{char: bits}' table + bit string. Crib-gated decoders + fixtures. Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep the decoders small, stdlib-only, normal imports.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse