-D22)**\", \"- **Base-N alphabet size\", \"\"\"- **Compressor under a text wrapper (D21-D22)** -- D21 single/TT = ONE std padded base64 string of a GZIP member\n  (`1f8b 08 00 00000000 02 03` = b64 `H4sIAAAAAAACA`); D22 = ONE std padded base64 string of a ZLIB stream `78da` -> b64\n  `eNo`/`eNp`/`eNq`/`eNr` (3rd char follows the first deflate byte: match `eN`). Mastery lines 21/22 = 36- / 20-char\n  padded fragments, each its OWN gzip member / zlib stream, side by side. Payload plain UTF-8; compressed bytes are not\n  printable, so printable-gated b64 branches reject them and rot-N returns garbage. Parse rule (D21 `_b64z`, took D22\n  unchanged): `[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]+={0,2}`, len%4 != 1 -> re-pad, urlsafe-decode -> sniff (`1f8b`, zlib, `BZh`,\n  `fd377a585a`) -> decompress -> UTF-8; whole blob BEFORE the numbered-line check + `register_free(\"b64z\", 21, ...)`.\n  Widen the zlib test to RFC 1950 (`b[0]&15==8`, `(b[0]<<8|b[1])%31==0`, FDICT -> `zdict=` crib) and try raw deflate\n  (`wbits=-15`); same rule for any wrapper (hex/b32/b85) and compressor (lzma-alone, zstd, lz4); re-run the full\n  decoder on the inflated text.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/ed_tech2.py && wc -l reference/techniques/warmups.md && sed -n 1,40p reference/techniques/warmups.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5540,"cache_read_input_tokens":94273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5540},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"830d579c-65ed-4429-b57e-18d79d768348","uuid":"2ba5daba-03b6-4a04-a85a-97778e9d8c15","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:33:21.044Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFgVgYcWMjBxaB3o2oU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016Ta6tV43YKwza5JW54f7Xv":{