e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\\n ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C G T only -> DNA 2-bit / codon\\n\")\nrep(\"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\\nTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \\\"Three rails\\\"); verify on the crib.\\n\",\n    \"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Title pun -> key: cipher + number = key (D18 \\\"Three rails\\\")\\n\")\nrep(\"\\\"Same ...\\\"/\\\"Another ...\\\"/\\\"This time ...\\\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned (order, alphabet, compressor).\\n\",\n    \"\\\"Same ...\\\"/\\\"Another ...\\\"/\\\"This time ...\\\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned; \\\"alphabet got bigger\\\" (D23) = base-N size\\n\")\nrep(\" tail); D19/D20 lines 19/20 each have their OWN BOM (LE and BE in one blob); D21/D22 lines 21/22 = own gzip / zlib streams.\",\n    \" tail); D19/D20 lines own BOM (LE+BE in one blob); D21/D22 own gzip/zlib streams; D23 own `<~..~>`. NEVER pre-decode a line\\n in place before decode_chunked (D23: plain `el-46` got ROT5 -> all NN wrong) -- register_free(name, day, fn) instead.\")\n\n# 5. JSON gaps\na = s.index(\"```json\\n\", s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")) + len(\"```json\\n\"); b = s.index(\"```\", a)\ngaps = json.loads(s[a:b]); byid = {g[\"id\"]: g for g in gaps}\nbuilt = {\"zlib-header-sweep\", \"flask-itsdangerous-cookie\", \"saml-redirect-deflate\", \"jwt-jose-segments\", \"pdf-filter-chain\",\n         \"xor-over-compressed-magic\", \"openssl-salted-envelope\", \"inflate-container-headers\", \"yenc-binhex\", \"rle-lzw-text-compression\"}\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"base85-variant-sweep\", \"concept\": \"Ascii85 knobs and the other 85-character alphabets: no delimiters, z/y shortcuts, wrapped lines, btoa, RFC1924/git b85, Z85, IPv6 RFC1924, a85 over a seen inner layer\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D24 (knob on D23 Adobe Ascii85 '<~...~>'). Build warmups_codecs.b85_any(t): strip whitespace/newlines; '<~..~>' -> a85decode(adobe=True) (append '~>' if only '<~' present); else a85decode(t) (z = 4 NULs) and a85decode(t, foldspaces=True) (y); b85decode (RFC1924/git/Python alphabet); Z85 via str.translate(Z85 alphabet -> b85 alphabet) then b85decode (pad to len%5==0 only for b85-style partials); btoa: lines between 'xbtoa Begin' and 'xbtoa End', a85 per line; IPv6 RFC1924 = 20-char token -> 16 bytes. Then magic sniff (gzip/zlib/bz2/xz/raw deflate) and decode_chunk on the output (hex/UTF-16/base64 inner layers), slug-gated. Register as a whole-blob candidate AND a free codec for 7-12 char Mastery fragments (each with own delimiters, as D23 line 23). Fixtures: every alphabet x delimited/bare x wrapped/unwrapped x plain/zlib/hex inner, plus 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92 (and base94/base95 printable-alphabet codecs)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next size up after D23's 85 ('The alphabet got bigger'). base92 (thenoviceoof): alphabet '!' + '#'..'_' + 'a'..'}' (91 symbols, '~' = empty string), 13-bit pairs -> 2 chars, trailing 6-bit -> 1 char. chepy has from_base92 but ship a stdlib decoder in warmups_codecs (+ encoder for fixtures). Also base94 (all of '!'..'~') bignum and base95 (incl. space) via the bignum-radix-alphabets decoder. Cues: printable minus double-quote and backtick, ~1.23 x length, may end '~'. Fixtures: single blob + 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base32768 / base2048 (dense Unicode base-N)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"End of the 'bigger alphabet' road: 16 bits per CJK/Hangul-like BMP/astral char (base65536), 15 bits per char (base32768, UTF-16-friendly), 11 bits per char (base2048, tweet-sized). Ship stdlib decoders with the block tables embedded (base65536: 256 blocks of 256 code points + padding blocks; base32768/base2048: repertoire strings from the reference implementations) or guard chepy from_base65536 as an optional import. Cue: ~55-60 dense non-ASCII chars for a 110-byte sentence, no spaces. Fixtures: each codec, single + Mastery fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"concept\": \"whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary-radix alphabet (base94/95 printable, base85/91 bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic catch-all for 'the alphabet got bigger' when no 4/5-chunk codec fits. For candidate alphabets (string.printable subsets: '!'..'~' (94), ' '..'~' (95), b85/a85/Z85/base91/base62/base58 alphabets, and ''.join(sorted(set(t)))), compute n = big-endian digit value, n.to_bytes(), also little-endian digit order; accept only UTF-8 text with the slug. Also leading-zero-symbol convention (base58 style). Cap at 2000 chars to stay < 50 ms. Fixtures: each alphabet x big/little digit order, single + fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base256-glyph-bytes\", \"concept\": \"one glyph per byte from a 256-symbol set: Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji, cp437/Latin-1 printable maps, U+0100+byte offset blocks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Alphabet as big as a byte'. Detect: every char non-ASCII and in ONE contiguous block (or the base256emoji table), count == 105-115. Decode: bytes(ord(c) - block_start) when all fall in a 256-wide window; base256emoji via its published 256-emoji table; cp437 via bytes(t.encode('cp437')) reversal. Then UTF-8 + slug gate, else feed bytes back to decode_chunk (inner layer). Fixtures: Braille-bytes, U+0100 offset, base256emoji, cp437.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base122-dense-utf8\", \"concept\": \"base122 (7-bit packing into UTF-8 with 2-byte illegal-char escapes) and similar dense UTF-8 packings\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Base-122 (kevinAlbs): 7-bit groups as 1-byte UTF-8; the 6 'illegal' values (0, 10, 13, 34, 38, 92) go into 2-byte 110sssxx 10xxxxxx sequences with the next 7 bits. Ship a stdlib decoder + encoder. Cue: valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII control-free text with \\\\xc2-\\\\xdf lead bytes, ~1.14 x the byte length, artifact may be bytes not text (read raw). Fixtures: single + fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bech32-base58check\", \"concept\": \"checksummed base-N encodings: base58check, bech32 / bech32m, Ripple / Flickr base58 alphabets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Crypto-address dress for base-N. bech32: 'hrp' + '1' + data in 'qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l' (5-bit), last 6 chars checksum -> regroup 5->8 bits (drop padding); verify polymod with const 1 (bech32) or 0x2bc830a3 (bech32m). base58check: base58 decode, strip 1 version byte + 4 checksum bytes (sha256d). Ripple alphabet 'rpshnaf39wBUDNEGHJKLM4PQRST7VWXYZ2bcdeCg65jkm8oFqi1tuvAxyz', Flickr = lowercase-first. Fixtures for each, crib-gated.\"},\n {\"id\": \"mastery-line-routing\", \"concept\": \"Mastery: every day's codec must claim its RAW line inside decode_chunked / _joint_free\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery lost its first submit (113/113 sets: right slug words, wrong NN, every digit +5): the solver pre-decoded line 23 ('<~..~>' -> 'el-46') in place, and the joint free-codec search -- which has no identity option -- gave the plain line a digit ROT5. Rule: never rewrite numbered lines before decode_chunked; add the day's codec via register_free(name, day, fn) (gated to its own charset/delimiters) or decode_chunk. Before any timed start, print one set's joined sentence and check the slug digits against the single-solve shape. Same fields wrong on every set = one line's routing.\"},\n]\norder_p1 = [\"base85-variant-sweep\", \"base92\", \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"base65536\", \"mastery-line-routing\", \"byte-family-mastery-cost\"]\nfor g in new:\n    byid[g[\"id\"]] = g\nbyid[\"byte-family-mastery-cost\"][\"detail\"] = byid[\"byte-family-mastery-cost\"][\"detail\"].replace(\n    \"profile per set if D23 grows it further.\", \"profile per set if it grows; D23 (113 x 23) solved in 1.2 s.\")\nfor gid in built:\n    if gid in byid and byid[gid][\"action\"] == \"prebuild\":\n        del byid[gid]\nfor gid in (\"serialization-wrappers\", \"zalgo-combining-strip\"):\n    byid[gid][\"priority\"] = 3 if gid == \"zalgo-combining-strip\" else 2\nbyid[\"serialization-wrappers\"][\"detail\"] += \" Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep it stdlib-only, normal imports, no deserialization.\"\nbyid[\"zalgo-combining-strip\"][\"detail\"] += \" Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false).\"\ndel byid[\"base92\"] if False else None\n# drop old note duplicates of upgraded ids already replaced via byid; order list\nrest = [g for gid, g in byid.items() if gid not in order_p1]\nrest.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])\nout = [byid[x] for x in order_p1] + rest\ns = s[:a] + \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in out) + \"\\n]\\n\" + s[b:]\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py && echo ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3827,"cache_read_input_tokens":105102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3827},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"830d579c-65ed-4429-b57e-18d79d768348","uuid":"61bf7b92-1544-4a6b-984c-08b67df8ee42","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:34:52.320Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFivmi6DPCSYJVqLFQx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XHzz7tvo4CbLT5EeLv43bY":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np = \"reference/coverage/warmups.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new, n=1):\n    global s\n    c = s.count(old); assert c == n, (c, old[:90]); s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# 1. narrative\ni = s.index(\"RHYTHM since D19:\"); j = s.index(\"Status legend:\")\ns = s[:i] + \"\"\"RHYTHM since D19: day N opens a family, day N+1 turns ONE knob (D19 LE -> D20 BE, D21 gzip -> D22 zlib). D23 opened a\nnew family as predicted, but not a web wrapper: \"The alphabet got bigger. Adobe might recognize the neighbors.\" /\n\"Eighty-Five Alive\" = ASCII85 in Adobe `<~ ... ~>` delimiters, ONE layer, plain UTF-8 inside (143 B single, 141 B TT;\nMastery line 23 = an 11-char `<~XXXXXXX~>` per fragment, own delimiters). The pun names the alphabet SIZE (16 -> 32 ->\n64 -> 85 \"got bigger\"), the variant (\"Adobe\" = PostScript/PDF Ascii85) and the armor (\"neighbors\" = `<~` `~>`).\nSo D24 is most likely the KNOB on Ascii85: another 85-alphabet (RFC1924 / git / Python `b85`, ZeroMQ Z85, btoa\n`xbtoa Begin`, IPv6 RFC1924), no delimiters, `z`/`y` shortcuts, line-wrapped armor, or Ascii85 over a seen inner layer\n(PDF ASCII85Decode + FlateDecode is prebuilt); or the alphabet growing again: basE91 / base92 / base94-95 bignum /\nbase100 emoji / base122 / base2048-32768-65536 / 256-glyph byte maps. Expect a \"Same ...\"/\"Bigger still\"/\"Even more\nneighbors\" style callback. Every one of those is keyless -- the charset fingerprint + crib slug gate is the whole job.\nSnapshot 2026-10-23 (after D23; every prebuild gap from the D22 list is built except serialization-wrappers and\nzalgo-combining-strip (1 failed attempt each) and rle-lzw-text-compression / middle-endian-pdp (given up); new base-N\nqueue below).\n\n\"\"\" + s[j:]\n\n# 2. table rows\nrep(\"| 29 | base85 RFC1924 / ascii85 (`<~ ~>`) | prebuilt wc:base85, ascii85, ascii85-adobe | yes | `!`-`u` (+`z`) / `0-9A-Za-z!#$%&()*+-;<=>?@^_{|}~`, x1.25 | `base64.a85decode`/`b85decode` | med: base-N progression |\",\n    \"| 29 | base85 RFC1924 / ascii85 (`<~ ~>`) | seen D23 (Adobe Ascii85 `<~...~>`, plain UTF-8 inside, no `z`, no wraps; Mastery line 23 = `<~XXXXXXX~>` per fragment; D23 solver `_a85` + `register_free(\\\"a85\\\",23)`); RFC1924 `b85`/no-delimiter a85 prebuilt wc:base85, ascii85 | yes | `<~`...`~>` around `!`-`u` (+`z`/`y`) / `0-9A-Za-z!#$%&()*+-;<=>?@^_{|}~`, x1.25 | `base64.a85decode(t, adobe=True)` (needs the closing `~>`) / `b85decode` | done (Mastery line 23); other 85 alphabets / armors -> row 157 (high: D24 knob) |\")\nrep(\"| 30 | Z85 (ZeroMQ) | prebuilt tgt:z85 | yes | `0-9a-zA-Z.-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$#`, len%5==0 | `basenc --z85 -d` (needs len%4 data); pyzmq z85 | low |\",\n    \"| 30 | Z85 (ZeroMQ) | prebuilt tgt:z85 | yes | `0-9a-zA-Z.-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$#`, len%5==0 | `basenc --z85 -d` (needs len%4 data); pyzmq z85 | high: the most likely D24 \\\"other 85\\\" knob |\")\nrep(\"| 31 | basE91 | prebuilt tgt:base91 | yes | 91 printable, no `'-\\\\` space, x1.23 | chepy from_base91 | med |\",\n    \"| 31 | basE91 | prebuilt tgt:base91 | yes | 91 printable, no `'-\\\\` space, x1.23 | chepy from_base91 | high: \\\"alphabet got bigger\\\" again |\")\nrep(\"| 32 | base92 | gap | yes |\", \"| 32 | base92 | gap (gap base92) | yes |\")\nrep(\"| chepy from_base92; CyberChef From Base92 | low |\", \"| chepy from_base92; CyberChef From Base92 | med-high: next size up |\")\nrep(\"| 33 | base100 / emoji | prebuilt tgt:base100-emoji |\", \"| 33 | base100 / emoji | prebuilt tgt:base100-emoji |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| per 4-byte emoji | med: \\\"Hundred\\\"/emoji pun |\", \"| per 4-byte emoji | med-high: \\\"Hundred\\\"/emoji, alphabet growth |\")\nrep(\"| 34 | base65536 / base2048 / base32768 | gap | yes |\", \"| 34 | base65536 / base2048 / base32768 | gap (gap base65536) | yes |\")\nrep(\"| chepy from_base65536; pip base2048 | low |\", \"| chepy from_base65536; pip base2048 | med: end of the \\\"bigger alphabet\\\" road |\")\nfor gid in [\"zlib-header-sweep\", \"flask-itsdangerous-cookie\", \"saml-redirect-deflate\", \"jwt-jose-segments\", \"pdf-filter-chain\",\n            \"xor-over-compressed-magic\", \"openssl-salted-envelope\", \"inflate-container-headers\", \"yenc-binhex\"]:\n    rep(f\"gap (gap {gid})\", f\"prebuilt tgt:{gid}\")\nrep(\"D21 solver `_b64z` sniff is `0x78`-only (prebuilt tgt:zlib-header-sweep)\", \"D21 solver `_b64z` sniff is `0x78`-only (fix: prebuilt tgt:zlib-header-sweep)\")\n\n# 3. new rows after 156\nk = s.index(\"| 156 |\"); e = s.index(\"\\n\", k) + 1\ns = s[:e] + \"\"\"| 157 | Ascii85 knobs / other 85-alphabets: no `<~ ~>`, `z` (4 NULs) and `y` (4 spaces) shortcuts, line-wrapped at 75/76/80, whitespace inside, btoa (`xbtoa Begin` ... `xbtoa End N n E S R` trailer), RFC1924/git/Python `b85` (`0-9A-Za-z!#$%&()*+-;<=>?@^_\\\\`{|}~`), Z85, IPv6 RFC1924 (20-char address), a85 over a seen inner layer (hex/UTF-16/gzip/zlib) | gap (gap base85-variant-sweep) | yes | charset of 85 printables; delimiters/trailer; length%5 in {0,2,3,4}; Z85 has `.` `:` `[` `]` and no `,` `;` `_` | `a85decode(t, adobe=..)`, `b85decode`, Z85 via `str.translate` to the b85 alphabet then `b85decode`; btoa = a85 per line, check the trailer; then magic sniff + `decode_chunk` | high: D24 knob on D23 |\n| 158 | whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary radix alphabet (base94 `!`-`~`, base95 incl. space, base85/91 as bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset) | gap (gap bignum-radix-alphabets) | yes | printable soup with no 4/5-chunk structure; length ~ 110*8/log2(N) | `n = sum(i*N**k)`; `n.to_bytes((n.bit_length()+7)//8,'big')`; try sorted(set(t)) and the standard alphabets; crib gate | med: \"bigger alphabet\" generalised |\n| 159 | base122 / other dense UTF-8 byte packings (7 bits per byte, 2-byte \"illegal\" sequences) | gap (gap base122-dense-utf8) | yes | valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII with `\\\\xc2`-`\\\\xdf` two-byte chars, ~1.14 x length | spec decoder (strip high bits, re-pack 7-bit groups) | low-med |\n| 160 | 256-glyph byte maps: one glyph per byte (Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji (multiformats), cp437 / Latin-1 printable map, `U+0100+byte`) | gap (gap base256-glyph-bytes) | yes | non-ASCII glyphs from ONE block, count = text length (110-115) | `bytes(ord(c)-base for c in t)` / table lookup | med: \"alphabet as big as a byte\" |\n| 161 | checksummed base-N: base58check (version byte + 4-byte SHA-256d checksum), bech32/bech32m (`hrp1` + `qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l` 5-bit groups + 6-char checksum), Ripple/Flickr base58 alphabets | gap (gap bech32-base58check) | yes | `bc1`/`hrp1` prefix, the bech32 charset; base58 with leading `1`s | regroup 5->8 bits after dropping hrp + checksum; base58 decode then strip version/checksum | low-med |\n\"\"\"\n\n# 4. recognition cues\nrep(\" ! .. u (+z), maybe <~ ~> ......... ascii85;  RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\\\ ]) -> base85; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85\\n\",\n    \" <~ ... ~> around ! .. u ......... ASCII85 (D23): a85decode(t,adobe=True); no <~ -> a85decode (z = 4 NULs);\\n   RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\\\ ]) -> b85decode; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85; xbtoa Begin -> btoa\\n\")\nrep(\" ~all printable, no ' - \\\\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \\\" ` -> base92\\n\",\n    \" ~all printable, no ' - \\\\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \\\" ` -> base92;  no chunk structure -> bignum radix\\n\")\n# trim: merge two short lines to stay <= 60\nrep(\" dotted quads / #RRGGBB / 4e69:6365 . IPv4 / colour / IPv6 bytes;  base64-ish that won't decode -> undo rev/rot13/atbash 1st (U4fV = rot13 H4sI)\\n only A D F G X (V) -> ADFGX/ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  only A C G T -> DNA 2-bit / codon\\n\",\n    \" dotted quads/#RRGGBB/4e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\\n ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C G T only -> DNA 2-bit / codon\\n\")\nrep(\"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\\nTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \\\"Three rails\\\"); verify on the crib.\\n\",\n    \"WORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Title pun -> key: cipher + number = key (D18 \\\"Three rails\\\")\\n\")\nrep(\"\\\"Same ...\\\"/\\\"Another ...\\\"/\\\"This time ...\\\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned (order, alphabet, compressor).\\n\",\n    \"\\\"Same ...\\\"/\\\"Another ...\\\"/\\\"This time ...\\\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned; \\\"alphabet got bigger\\\" (D23) = base-N size\\n\")\nrep(\" tail); D19/D20 lines 19/20 each have their OWN BOM (LE and BE in one blob); D21/D22 lines 21/22 = own gzip / zlib streams.\",\n    \" tail); D19/D20 lines own BOM (LE+BE in one blob); D21/D22 own gzip/zlib streams; D23 own `<~..~>`. NEVER pre-decode a line\\n in place before decode_chunked (D23: plain `el-46` got ROT5 -> all NN wrong) -- register_free(name, day, fn) instead.\")\n\n# 5. JSON gaps\na = s.index(\"```json\\n\", s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")) + len(\"```json\\n\"); b = s.index(\"```\", a)\ngaps = json.loads(s[a:b]); byid = {g[\"id\"]: g for g in gaps}\nbuilt = {\"zlib-header-sweep\", \"flask-itsdangerous-cookie\", \"saml-redirect-deflate\", \"jwt-jose-segments\", \"pdf-filter-chain\",\n         \"xor-over-compressed-magic\", \"openssl-salted-envelope\", \"inflate-container-headers\", \"yenc-binhex\", \"rle-lzw-text-compression\"}\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"base85-variant-sweep\", \"concept\": \"Ascii85 knobs and the other 85-character alphabets: no delimiters, z/y shortcuts, wrapped lines, btoa, RFC1924/git b85, Z85, IPv6 RFC1924, a85 over a seen inner layer\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D24 (knob on D23 Adobe Ascii85 '<~...~>'). Build warmups_codecs.b85_any(t): strip whitespace/newlines; '<~..~>' -> a85decode(adobe=True) (append '~>' if only '<~' present); else a85decode(t) (z = 4 NULs) and a85decode(t, foldspaces=True) (y); b85decode (RFC1924/git/Python alphabet); Z85 via str.translate(Z85 alphabet -> b85 alphabet) then b85decode (pad to len%5==0 only for b85-style partials); btoa: lines between 'xbtoa Begin' and 'xbtoa End', a85 per line; IPv6 RFC1924 = 20-char token -> 16 bytes. Then magic sniff (gzip/zlib/bz2/xz/raw deflate) and decode_chunk on the output (hex/UTF-16/base64 inner layers), slug-gated. Register as a whole-blob candidate AND a free codec for 7-12 char Mastery fragments (each with own delimiters, as D23 line 23). Fixtures: every alphabet x delimited/bare x wrapped/unwrapped x plain/zlib/hex inner, plus 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92 (and base94/base95 printable-alphabet codecs)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next size up after D23's 85 ('The alphabet got bigger'). base92 (thenoviceoof): alphabet '!' + '#'..'_' + 'a'..'}' (91 symbols, '~' = empty string), 13-bit pairs -> 2 chars, trailing 6-bit -> 1 char. chepy has from_base92 but ship a stdlib decoder in warmups_codecs (+ encoder for fixtures). Also base94 (all of '!'..'~') bignum and base95 (incl. space) via the bignum-radix-alphabets decoder. Cues: printable minus double-quote and backtick, ~1.23 x length, may end '~'. Fixtures: single blob + 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base32768 / base2048 (dense Unicode base-N)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"End of the 'bigger alphabet' road: 16 bits per CJK/Hangul-like BMP/astral char (base65536), 15 bits per char (base32768, UTF-16-friendly), 11 bits per char (base2048, tweet-sized). Ship stdlib decoders with the block tables embedded (base65536: 256 blocks of 256 code points + padding blocks; base32768/base2048: repertoire strings from the reference implementations) or guard chepy from_base65536 as an optional import. Cue: ~55-60 dense non-ASCII chars for a 110-byte sentence, no spaces. Fixtures: each codec, single + Mastery fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"concept\": \"whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary-radix alphabet (base94/95 printable, base85/91 bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic catch-all for 'the alphabet got bigger' when no 4/5-chunk codec fits. For candidate alphabets (string.printable subsets: '!'..'~' (94), ' '..'~' (95), b85/a85/Z85/base91/base62/base58 alphabets, and ''.join(sorted(set(t)))), compute n = big-endian digit value, n.to_bytes(), also little-endian digit order; accept only UTF-8 text with the slug. Also leading-zero-symbol convention (base58 style). Cap at 2000 chars to stay < 50 ms. Fixtures: each alphabet x big/little digit order, single + fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base256-glyph-bytes\", \"concept\": \"one glyph per byte from a 256-symbol set: Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji, cp437/Latin-1 printable maps, U+0100+byte offset blocks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Alphabet as big as a byte'. Detect: every char non-ASCII and in ONE contiguous block (or the base256emoji table), count == 105-115. Decode: bytes(ord(c) - block_start) when all fall in a 256-wide window; base256emoji via its published 256-emoji table; cp437 via bytes(t.encode('cp437')) reversal. Then UTF-8 + slug gate, else feed bytes back to decode_chunk (inner layer). Fixtures: Braille-bytes, U+0100 offset, base256emoji, cp437.\"},\n {\"id\": \"base122-dense-utf8\", \"concept\": \"base122 (7-bit packing into UTF-8 with 2-byte illegal-char escapes) and similar dense UTF-8 packings\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Base-122 (kevinAlbs): 7-bit groups as 1-byte UTF-8; the 6 'illegal' values (0, 10, 13, 34, 38, 92) go into 2-byte 110sssxx 10xxxxxx sequences with the next 7 bits. Ship a stdlib decoder + encoder. Cue: valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII control-free text with \\\\xc2-\\\\xdf lead bytes, ~1.14 x the byte length, artifact may be bytes not text (read raw). Fixtures: single + fragment.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bech32-base58check\", \"concept\": \"checksummed base-N encodings: base58check, bech32 / bech32m, Ripple / Flickr base58 alphabets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Crypto-address dress for base-N. bech32: 'hrp' + '1' + data in 'qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l' (5-bit), last 6 chars checksum -> regroup 5->8 bits (drop padding); verify polymod with const 1 (bech32) or 0x2bc830a3 (bech32m). base58check: base58 decode, strip 1 version byte + 4 checksum bytes (sha256d). Ripple alphabet 'rpshnaf39wBUDNEGHJKLM4PQRST7VWXYZ2bcdeCg65jkm8oFqi1tuvAxyz', Flickr = lowercase-first. Fixtures for each, crib-gated.\"},\n {\"id\": \"mastery-line-routing\", \"concept\": \"Mastery: every day's codec must claim its RAW line inside decode_chunked / _joint_free\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery lost its first submit (113/113 sets: right slug words, wrong NN, every digit +5): the solver pre-decoded line 23 ('<~..~>' -> 'el-46') in place, and the joint free-codec search -- which has no identity option -- gave the plain line a digit ROT5. Rule: never rewrite numbered lines before decode_chunked; add the day's codec via register_free(name, day, fn) (gated to its own charset/delimiters) or decode_chunk. Before any timed start, print one set's joined sentence and check the slug digits against the single-solve shape. Same fields wrong on every set = one line's routing.\"},\n]\norder_p1 = [\"base85-variant-sweep\", \"base92\", \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"base65536\", \"mastery-line-routing\", \"byte-family-mastery-cost\"]\nfor g in new:\n    byid[g[\"id\"]] = g\nbyid[\"byte-family-mastery-cost\"][\"detail\"] = byid[\"byte-family-mastery-cost\"][\"detail\"].replace(\n    \"profile per set if D23 grows it further.\", \"profile per set if it grows; D23 (113 x 23) solved in 1.2 s.\")\nfor gid in built:\n    if gid in byid and byid[gid][\"action\"] == \"prebuild\":\n        del byid[gid]\nfor gid in (\"serialization-wrappers\", \"zalgo-combining-strip\"):\n    byid[gid][\"priority\"] = 3 if gid == \"zalgo-combining-strip\" else 2\nbyid[\"serialization-wrappers\"][\"detail\"] += \" Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep it stdlib-only, normal imports, no deserialization.\"\nbyid[\"zalgo-combining-strip\"][\"detail\"] += \" Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false).\"\ndel byid[\"base92\"] if False else None\n# drop old note duplicates of upgraded ids already replaced via byid; order list\nrest = [g for gid, g in byid.items() if gid not in order_p1]\nrest.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])\nout = [byid[x] for x in order_p1] + rest\ns = s[:a] + \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in out) + \"\\n]\\n\" + s[b:]\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py && echo ok"}}}
