{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFwF2eRqhtH2YbK7EPy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both warmups files for day 23.\n\n- **`reference/techniques/warmups.md` (221 lines, a bit over the ~200 target):**\n  - **Day 23 entry:** \"Eighty-Five Alive\" was Ascii85 inside Adobe's `<~ ~>` delimiters, one layer. The Single Solve was CORRECT in about 36 s with one `base64.a85decode(t, adobe=True)` call, and the Time Trial in 5.1 s.\n  - **Mastery failure:** the first Mastery submit (113 sets × 23 lines) got the slug words right but every number wrong (each digit +5). The solver had already decoded line 23 to plain text before handing the blob to `decode_chunked`. The joint free-codec search then applied a digit ROT5 to that plain line. The fix was to remove that early decode and let the registered `a85` codec read the raw line. It went CORRECT on the same attempt, with a 1.2 s solve.\n  - **Variant axis:** added \"Base-N alphabet size / armor (D23)\" with the shapes seen (143 B single, 141 B TT, 11-char Mastery lines each with their own delimiters) and a parse rule covering the other 85-character alphabets. Also added a cue-table row, a new Pitfall (\"never pre-decode Mastery lines\"), and updated the pun list, family rhythm, Mastery line list and clocks. To stay near ~200 lines I folded D22 into the D14-22 summary and shortened the older axes.\n- **`reference/coverage/warmups.md`:**\n  - Row 29 is now `seen D23`, and the narrative forecasts D24 as a knob on Ascii85 (Z85, RFC1924 `b85`, btoa, no delimiters, `z`/`y` shortcuts) or a still-bigger alphabet.\n  - Nine already-built rows were still marked `gap`; I corrected them to `prebuilt`, and added rows 157-161.\n  - The cue block is now 59 lines; it was already 61-62 before today.\n  - The gaps JSON is valid and has the same keys. I removed the built prebuild gaps and added 7 new ones: `base85-variant-sweep`, `bignum-radix-alphabets`, `base256-glyph-bytes`, `base122-dense-utf8` and `bech32-base58check`, plus `base92` and `base65536` changed from notes to prebuilds. That leaves 9 unbuilt prebuild gaps (8 required). I also added a priority-1 note, `mastery-line-routing`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":778,"cache_read_input_tokens":137146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":778},"output_tokens":834,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"830d579c-65ed-4429-b57e-18d79d768348","uuid":"846903fa-29c2-4198-a0e8-8abacb65e372","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:36:35.135Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFwEf5Dabp5NZiUPENu"}
